    <!-- About Section -->
    <section id="about" class="mb-20 md:mb-24">
      <h3 class="font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-[0.25em] mb-8">About - me and my wild gems</h3>
      
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-start">
        <!-- Photos -->
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <img src="/img/beau.jpg" alt="Parent and child" class="col-span-2 w-full aspect-square object-cover border-4 border-neutral-900 shadow-brutalist-green-lg">
          <img src="/img/bigs.jpg" alt="Kids together" class="w-full aspect-square object-cover border-4 border-neutral-900 shadow-brutalist-pink">
          <img src="/img/family.jpg" alt="Family" class="w-full aspect-square object-cover border-4 border-neutral-900 shadow-brutalist-blue">
        </div>
        
        <!-- Content -->
        <!-- Content -->
        <div class="text-neutral-700 space-y-5 leading-relaxed">
          <p>I'm Sacha. I have three kids. We homeschool in Reno, NV.</p>
          
          <p>I was a perfect student with a strong math and stats background. Then I spent 10 years as an education hacker and super tutor—outside the system, by choice. Now I run a data strategy company and share what we're building here because I think it might lessen some suffering and add some joy to this hard, rewarding path.</p>
          
          <p>We homeschool because our family naturally beats to our own drum. My husband led the charge. We both knew we could provide something better for our kids based on our values. Having that control to craft their education? Liberating. Fun.</p>
          
          <p>My kids learn through hiking, farming, martial arts, soccer, and life. Kai reads beginner books and played his first soccer league. Rose dances through everything with wild creativity. Beau, the third-born, keeps up with both of them somehow.</p>
          
          <p>I question things. I lead with kindness. I bake really well (but only for people I like).</p>
          
          <p>This site is what's working—and what's not—for us. Take what helps. Leave the rest.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

